# =============================================================================
# Myunivokai Web — Environment File (.env.example)
# =============================================================================
# Used by apps/myunivokai-personalization/docker-compose-local.yaml (standalone mode)
# and also by Next.js when running with `npm run dev` on the host.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# =============================================================================

# --- Frontend ---
# The browser uses this URL to reach the API Gateway.
# Use http://localhost:41800 for local development.
# In production (Render/Vercel), set to the Gateway's public URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_BASE_URL=http://localhost:41800

# --- Renderer rollout ---
# LEAVE THIS UNSET. Unset ships WebGPURenderer to EVERY visitor, which means its
# WebGL2 backend on the roughly 20% of browsers with no WebGPU. That backend
# blocks the main thread for 13.6 s on the forest's first mount against
# WebGLRenderer's 3.6 s. The cost is known and was accepted on 2026-09-19.
#
# The two values that DO something, in the order a person reaches for them:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_NODE_RENDERER=where-webgpu-is-real
#                              The middle setting. WebGPURenderer only where
#                              navigator.gpu reports a hardware adapter; every-
#                              body else gets WebGLRenderer. Keeps the WebGPU
#                              win and gives up the WebGL2 first mount. Reach
#                              for this BEFORE the kill switch.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_NODE_RENDERER=0
#                              Kill switch. Also 'off', 'false', 'no',
#                              'disabled', any case. WebGLRenderer for everyone.
#
# Anything unrecognised means the default, which is the aggressive setting — so
# a value typed to disable this that is not in the list above will NOT disable
# it. Use one of the spellings above.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined by Next AT BUILD TIME, so changing either one needs a
# rebuild and redeploy of the frontend, not just an environment edit. And note
# that .env.local in this repository does not reach the Vercel deployment, which
# overrides env from its own dashboard — the shipped default lives in
# rendererSelection.ts for that reason.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NODE_RENDERER=
